claimed: okay-script-runtime -- extend okay-script for the real goal (operator, 2026-09-03): generate a .md file at RUNTIME, compile+run it in-process, and have it come up as a live web app (frontend+backend), e.g. for spinning up a storefront, all inside the running JVM -- no CLI, no build step. Concretely: (1) explicit Classpath param instead of always the ambient System classpath, so a script can be given exactly okay-ui/okay-jetty/etc without depending on the callers own classpath; (2) //> using dep directive parsing + Coursier resolution at runtime, so a generated script can name an extra library it needs; (3) isolate the scripts classloader (platform-classloader parent) so multiple runtime-compiled apps do not collide. Blocking/lifecycle of a live server is the CALLERS concern (invoke run on a background thread/fiber) -- not solved inside ScalaScript itself.
